It's fairly well establishd that you can give the priest in a 
co-aligined temple 400*your_level of gold and be granted some 
intrisic armor class.  You can also lose this AC if you kill a 
priest in a temple.  (happened to me on the first level of 
gennehom (sp).  

The basic thing is, if you're high enough level to have a ton of 
gold, then 'buying' intrisic AC from a priest will get you mabye 
a maximum of -19 intrisic AC.  Then you have to get some more gold, 
maybe by killing the priest, then find another priest and start all 
over again.  WHAT A PAIN!

So here's what I did.  (Sorry it's rather involved, but you know 
this game!)

1. Found a co-aligned temple with a priest in it on level 19. (This 
is after my quest.  In fact, I had already visited the first level of hell.)

2. Found the magic portal to Fort Ludios (sp) there on the same level. (lucky).

3. After clearing out the fort, went swimming in the moat with several 
scrolls to turn them into blank scrolls.  (I could have just dipped them, 
but I had an amulet of Magic breathing and it is more fun to go swimming 
-as long as you remove your rustables.)

4. Gathered all the tools in the whole fort. (got a lot of bugules) 
(kicking works great for gathering things into piles.  Except for armor
and bodies: the bodies deteriorate anyway and the armor you can tediously
pick up and move.)  Polypiled evereything until I got a magic marker.  
(Had previously used the Wand of Wishing in the fort to get the PYEC and a
Blessed Wand of Polymorph)

5. Cursed the magic marker by dipping it into unholy H2O and wrote 2 scrolls 
of genocide. (cursed, of course.) (contrary to popular belief, It didn't take
30 charges per scroll.)

6. Stripped off all of my armor, but held on to my sword, firebrand, and went
to an empty room. There I read the first scroll and summoned about 8 Wraiths.
I let them hit me over and over until I went down from level 24 to level 8. 
(Lost my intrisic teleport in the process, which surprised me, but oh well.) 
(My hit points also went from about 209 to 98 in the process.  Bummer.)

7. Gathered up the three Wraith corpses (leftovers) and stuffed them into an
ice box.

8. Went back to my empty room and genocided Nurses.  This generated about 8
nurses which, as soon as I went empty handed, started building up my hit 
points again.  They did typical Nurse things until my HP were back up to 
about 200.

9. Now that I was at level 8, it only cost me 3200 gp to get a bonus to 
my intirisc AC instead of costing 9600.  That means that for my measly 
81,000 gold pieces I could get 25 lowerings of my AC instead of just 8!  
What a deal!

10. Still, having an intrisic AC of - 15 is nice, but in the tradition 
of greed, I wanted MORE!  So I Went to the room I had turned into my 
workshop (next to the temple) and dropped all my posessions  (ALL of them) 
on a square marked Elbereth.  Picked up the wand of polymorph and moved off 
the marked square.  (I had Intrisic Polymorph control, so I didn't need
a ring.)

11. Zapped myself with the wand, turned myself into a leprechaun, and 
visited the priest.  One hit and I had all the priest's gold, and a very 
angry priest. Obviously, I left the room ASAP!  Since I had been hit a 
couple of times by the priest, I was now back in my original form.

12. Dropped all the gold, put on my (rather substantial) armor, and visited 
the priest again. He was still ticked at me, so I got close and zapped a 
charm monster, which mellowed him out considerably.  So I went back to my
workshop and repeaded the process until I had an intirsic of about -66.  
No doubt I could have gotten more, but I was getting tired of the whole 
(rather tedious) routine.



That's what I did anyway.  Really all you *need* for this is some gold, 
a wand of polymorph, and some way of taming an angry priest.  If you want 
to lower your level to make it easier, you can do the genocide wraiths 
thing.  And of course, the genocide nurse thing can be done ad-nauseum.    

Maybe if you're lucky, next week I'll tell you what happens when you offer 
the corpse of death on the neutral altar of the endgame.


